    "lem-nrqmx-determinant-curvature-is-trace": {
      "citations": [
        {
          "fact": "A1",
          "source": "def-countable-choice",
          "source_section": "Definition",
          "quote": "The **Axiom of Countable Choice**, written $\\mathrm{AC}_\\omega$, is the following\nstatement.",
          "uses": [
            "1.1"
          ]
        },
        {
          "fact": "F1",
          "source": "def-nrqmx-determinant-line-projector",
          "source_section": "Definition",
          "quote": "Let $M$ be a smooth manifold, let $r\\ge1$, and let $P:M\\to M_r(\\mathbb C)$ be a $C^2$ orthogonal projector of constant rank $m$, with $1\\le m\\le r$. Its image bundle is $E_P=\\{(x,v):P(x)v=v\\}$, with the projected connection $\\nabla s=P\\,ds$ of [[def-nrqmx-smooth-projector-bundle]]. The **determinant line bundle** is the complex line bundle",
          "uses": [
            "1.1"
          ]
        },
        {
          "fact": "F2",
          "source": "lem-nrqmx-determinant-line-projector-well-defined",
          "source_section": "Statement",
          "quote": "For the projector of [[def-nrqmx-determinant-line-projector]], $Q(x)=\\bigwedge^mP(x)$ is a $C^2$ orthogonal projector of rank one. Its range is exactly $\\det E_P(x)=\\bigwedge^m\\operatorname{im}P(x)$, so these ranges form the determinant line bundle.",
          "uses": [
            "1.1"
          ]
        },
        {
          "fact": "F3",
          "source": "thm-nrqmx-berry-projector-curvature",
          "source_section": "Statement",
          "quote": "Assume Countable Choice. Let $M$, $d$, and $P$ satisfy [[def-nrqmx-smooth-projector-bundle]], with constant rank $r$. The curvature of the projected connection $\\nabla=P\\,d$, as an endomorphism-valued two-form on $\\mathbb C^d$, is\n$$F=P(dP\\wedge dP)P.$$\nFor any local $C^2$ orthonormal frame $V:U\\to\\mathbb C^{d\\times r}$ with $V^*V=I_r$ and $P=VV^*$, its connection matrix $A=V^*dV$ is anti-Hermitian and its curvature matrix is $F_{\\mathrm{fr}}=dA+A\\wedge A=V^*FV$. If $V'=Vg$ for a $C^2$ map $g:U\\to U(r)$, then $A'=g^{-1}Ag+g^{-1}dg$ and $F'_{\\mathrm{fr}}=g^{-1}F_{\\mathrm{fr}}g$. Along every $C^2$ path, Kato transport is unitary and intertwines the endpoint projectors.",
          "uses": [
            "2.1"
          ]
        }
      ],
      "derivations": [
        {
          "id": "step-1-1",
          "claim": "Because the columns of $V$ are orthonormal, $w=v_1\\wedge\\cdots\\wedge v_m$ has unit norm and spans the determinant line. Differentiating by the product rule gives $dw=\\sum_j v_1\\wedge\\cdots\\wedge dv_j\\wedge\\cdots\\wedge v_m$. The projected connection applies $P$ to each differentiated factor. Since $P\\,dv_j=\\sum_a v_a A_{aj}$, each term with $a\\ne j$ vanishes from a repeated wedge factor, while the $a=j$ term is $A_{jj}w$. Summing gives $Qdw=(\\operatorname{tr}A)w$, so the determinant connection form is $a=\\operatorname{tr}A$.",
          "step": "1.1",
          "inputs": [
            "A1",
            "F1",
            "F2",
            "given",
            "algebra"
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "step-2-1",
          "claim": "A line connection with scalar one-form $a$ has curvature $da+a\\wedge a=da$, since a scalar one-form wedges with itself to zero. By [F3], $\\operatorname{tr}F=\\operatorname{tr}(dA)+\\operatorname{tr}(A\\wedge A)$. In coordinates, $\\operatorname{tr}(A\\wedge A)=\\sum_{i,j}A_{ij}\\wedge A_{ji}=0$: diagonal terms vanish and each off-diagonal pair cancels because one-forms anticommute. Therefore $da=d\\operatorname{tr}A=\\operatorname{tr}F_{\\mathrm{fr}}=\\operatorname{tr}(V^*FV)$. Finally, since $PFP=F$ and $VV^*=P$, cyclicity of finite-dimensional trace gives $\\operatorname{tr}(V^*FV)=\\operatorname{tr}(FVV^*)=\\operatorname{tr}(FP)=\\operatorname{tr}F$.",
          "step": "2.1",
          "inputs": [
            "F3",
            "step 1.1",
            "algebra"
          ]
        }
      ],
      "routine_steps": [],
      "boundaries": [
        {
          "case": "empty",
          "status": "checked",
          "evidence": "An empty frame domain has no local curvature claim; the statement is on each open set carrying a frame. See the item Statement or Definition."
        },
        {
          "case": "zero",
          "status": "checked",
          "evidence": "For a constant projector and constant frame, A=0 and both curvature expressions vanish. See the item Statement or Definition."
        },
        {
          "case": "one",
          "status": "checked",
          "evidence": "At m=1, tr A=A and the determinant-line connection is the original line connection. See the item Statement or Definition."
        },
        {
          "case": "degenerate",
          "status": "checked",
          "evidence": "Repeated eigenvalues within the rank-m bundle do not affect the frame computation. See the item Statement or Definition."
        },
        {
          "case": "endpoints",
          "status": "checked",
          "evidence": "The identity is local and applies up to any chart boundary where the stated C2 frame is defined. See the item Statement or Definition."
        },
